<article class="env-proposition" id="9F8E7C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9F8E7C">Proposition <span data-tag="9F8E7C">8.2.2.1</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a model category. Let $X$ be a cofibrant object of $\calC $, $Y$ a fibrant object of $\calC $, and $f,g: X \rightarrow Y$ two maps. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
For every cylinder object $X \coprod X \stackrel{j}{\rightarrow } C$, there exists a commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \coprod X \ar [rr]^{j} \ar [dr]^{(f,g)} &  &  C \ar [dl] \\ &  Y} \]
</div>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
There exists a cylinder object $X \coprod X \stackrel{j}{\rightarrow } C$ and a commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \coprod X \ar [rr]^{j} \ar [dr]^{(f,g)} &  &  C \ar [dl] \\ &  Y} \]
</div>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
For every path object $P \stackrel{p}{\rightarrow } Y \times Y$, there exists a commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [rr] \ar [dr]^{(f,g)} &  &  P \ar [dl]^{p} \\ &  Y \times Y} \]
</div>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(4)$"><p>
There exists a path object $P \stackrel{p}{\rightarrow } Y \times Y$ and a commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [rr] \ar [dr]^{(f,g)} &  &  P \ar [dl]^{p} \\ &  Y \times Y} \]
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>